-- mixtures that differ in any one proportion are different substances, proved. So the component list is
-- not the identity of a mixture, and an identity given by source and process -- which is what ECHA's
-- guidance makes the basis for a UVCB, and what its study found registrants supplying -- does not
-- determine the proportions and therefore does not determine the substance. With
-- provenance-not-identity that is the regulator's own conclusion twice over: no widely applicable
-- sameness criteria can be developed from what the dossiers hold.
mix-frac-differs : (I : Type 0) → (u : I) → (m : Mix I) → (n : Mix I) → (mx-frac I m u ≡ mx-frac I n u → Empty) → (m ≡ n → Empty)
mix-frac-differs I u m n no = λ p → no (λ i → mx-frac I (p i) u)
